    {id:"Q02",answer:"The Faction Mat sets starting power and combat-card draw; the Player Mat sets starting popularity, coins and two objective cards. On the map, place the character at home base and two workers, one on each of the two land-adjoined territories adjoining home. On the mats, place four mechs over Faction Mat abilities, six stars by the faction emblem, six technology cubes in Player Mat green boxes marked with a black square, four structures on matching Player Mat boxes, four recruits on bottom-row circular spaces, and the other six workers on Produce red rectangles. Put the action token beside the Player Mat ready for its first placement; leave one-time Faction Mat recruit spaces empty.",support:"supported",evidence:"Setup steps 3–4 list which mat sets each starting value and the starting positions for all pieces."},
